# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server environment — copy to `.env` and edit.
#
#   cp apps/server/.env.example apps/server/.env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and is loaded ONLY by the dev scripts
# (`pnpm dev` / `pnpm dev:clean`) via Node's `--env-file-if-exists`.
# The production entrypoint (`pnpm start`) does NOT read it — production
# config must come from the real environment.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Local development convenience ─────────────────────────────
#
# Skip device pairing while developing. With this set, requests arriving on
# 127.0.0.1/::1 are accepted without a credential and run as a `local-desktop`
# principal with all scopes.
#
# This CANNOT be turned on by accident in a real deployment. The server
# refuses to start (StartupSecurityError) if it is set while either:
#   * the listener is not loopback-only (GENERATORAI_BIND_HOST != 127.0.0.1), or
#   * NODE_ENV=production
# and `AuthService` independently re-checks `isLoopback` on every request, so
# a remote caller is rejected even if the flag is somehow on.
#
# Leave it commented out to develop against the real pairing flow.
#
# GENERATORAI_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_LOOPBACK=1


# ── Copilot auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave BOTH unset unless you have a specific reason.
#
# The Copilot CLI resolves the tenant from its own stored credentials
# (`copilot` → `/login`), including GHEC `*.ghe.com` hosts. Setting
# COPILOT_GH_HOST when the CLI already has a working credential has been
# observed to BREAK it — `models.list` then fails with "Not authenticated.
# Please authenticate first." and the provider drops out of the catalog.
#
# If you do set a host, keep COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN unset: a github.com token
# 401s against a `*.ghe.com` tenant. (VS Code injects COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN
# into spawned terminals, which is exactly that failure mode.)
#
# COPILOT_GH_HOST=https://your-tenant.ghe.com/
# COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN=


# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=3100
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# COPILOT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4.6

# Bind address. Anything other than loopback is a deliberate act and forces
# authentication on (see the fail-closed gates in composition/security.ts).
# GENERATORAI_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Ordered origins placed into pairing offers. Use HTTPS for browsers served
# from HTTPS; plain HTTP is accepted only for loopback or private LAN hosts.
# When omitted on a wildcard bind, private IPv4 interfaces are discovered.
# GENERATORAI_ADVERTISED_URLS=https://host.example.ts.net,http://192.168.1.20:3100


# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without one of these the secret store falls back to a mode-0600 key file,
# which is readable by any process running as this OS user. Required
# off-loopback or in production.
# GENERATORAI_SECRET_KEY=
# GENERATORAI_SECRET_PASSPHRASE=
